UID:dde1780ffcf3f668d7df5bdbc2f35cf39202026_10:43:34_AM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Animation Guest Speaker: Monica Davila - Storyboarding and Directing in Animation
LOCATION: Sign in to download the location
URL:https://sundevilcentral.eoss.asu.edu/rsvp?id=414895
DESCRIPTION:Join WIA at ASU for an in-person guest lecture with Monica Davila!\n\nMonica Davila is an award-winning director, storyboard artist, and illustrator who has worked at studios such as Nickelodeon, Disney Television Animation, Netflix, Titmouse, and more. She has storyboarded and directed projects for clients such as Mattel, The Pokemon Company International, and most recently directed the BT21 Happy Meal commercial and socials for McDonalds and W+K. She also teaches storyboarding at Concept Design Academy.\n\nMonica’s lecture will cover a variety of topics including how she became a storyboard artist and director, what the animation pipeline for a television show is like, the different roles in a production, what makes a strong storyboard portfolio, and much more. She will walk students through her own storyboard process, provide insights into the reality of being a working artist, review portfolios, and give constructive feedback to help students prepare to enter the animation industry.\n---\nEvent Details: https://sundevilcentral.eoss.asu.edu/rsvp?id=414895
END:VEVENT
